							<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Why does 10 pages of a textbook, PDF, or the Quran take longer than a novel?</strong> A paperback novel uses wide margins and familiar dialogue (~300 words/page). By contrast, a 10-page college textbook or academic PDF often packs 450–600 words per page plus charts and terminology, taking 25 to 45 minutes to study properly. Similarly, reading 10 pages of the Quran (Uthmani script) with careful pronunciation and reflection typically takes 15 to 25 minutes, depending on your familiarity with Arabic.
						</li>
						<li>
							<strong class="font-semibold text-ink">Is it normal if it takes me an hour to read 10 pages?</strong> Yes, if you are reading dense technical material, studying a foreign language, highlighting key points, or taking notes. For casual fiction, however, 10 pages per hour (~50 WPM) means you are either re-reading lines frequently or getting distracted.
